{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games","id":661921,"title":"What are your favorite house-rules for crossover games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-12T07:54:15-07:00","id":661921,"title":"What are your favorite house-rules for crossover games?","content":"What house rules do you use to make multi-species games workable/balanced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T09:32:20-07:00","id":662012,"title":"","content":"Haven't really had too personally. Anything in particular you're wondering about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T10:52:48-07:00","id":662052,"title":"","content":"No, just a general curiosity about different playstyles and attempts at creative workarounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T11:48:34-07:00","id":662073,"title":"","content":"Ok, cool<br /> <br /> is that to get them to work together as a Troupe? If so I usually create a common foe or purpose. Give Vamps a chance to manipulate the situation to create a deal with Caveats to hopefully strike an accord for mutual survival during and after the event. Also to test the Garous drive to uphold honor over gaining Glory.<br /> <br /> If you mean creating an all encompassing reality where everyone knows and understands the universe equally the same?... i've never done that but I guess a way would be take out everything WoD related to the mythos and origins of each splat and just say their conditions are what they are and they exist in the world as a possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T22:58:28-07:00","id":662700,"title":"","content":"For crossover games I would let vampires play ghoul characters during the day. That allows the other players to do things during the day without the vampire player having to sit around and twiddle his thumbs. If I were running V:tM with W:tA I would give vampires a bit of a physical boost so that if a fight were to occur, they could participate without being quickly destroyed or being a useless. Letting them soak aggravated damage with Stamina would be one such boost.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't address the topic of who is right or wrong in any cosmological sense. The is no need, the characters don't have access to the answers to big questions like that, the players don't need them either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T12:08:59-07:00","id":663331,"title":"","content":"My favourite is to simply NOT do it... and while that's more me being cheeky than helpful, it has some merit in regards to classic World of Darkness. By that I mean the various 'splats' are explicitly written to be soley populated by that 'splat'. This means only that crossover is a decent bit of headache for a Storyteller, but it can be quite worth the effort!<br /> <br /> The 'rule' I lean on most is to have fun, and I apply that to ALL members of the troupe (including the Storyteller!). Sometimes following that rule means throwing out the rules-as-written, but I find that it USUALLY expresses more as finding various forms of <i>flexibility</i> over slavish devotion to any 'canon' from a book. As <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\">Sergeant Brother</a></b> suggests \u2013 and I outright state \u2013 the rules may need a tweak (if not an entire reinterpretation) to make any crossover work. Let's face it, a player character ghost is weak in our world when compared to a vampire, but even a puissant Kindred such as Augustus Giovanni can be smashed by the forces of the Underworld if he's not careful!<br /> <br /> The fact of the matter is that the Storyteller needs to know what the players want, weigh that against what the Storyteller can do, and that's where negotiation comes in. Does the player want a mummy to hang out with vampires 'coz there's a great story to be told? Does the Storyteller think it can be done with a Setite instead? Why does it NEED to be one of the Amenti, anyway? It's a lot more nuanced than simple 'power gamer' versus the rest of us in most cases, but I know those things happen. Toe to toe, a recently awakened mage is no match for a Garou right after her first change, and while that's not the point of MY troupe's games, such 'white room combat' IS fun from time to time. The player who joined our <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> chronicle playing a Bastet pawn shoppe owner had legitimate reasons for wanting that character, and after some work, we made it happen without too much trouble. We DID work, and that made all the difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T15:52:39-07:00","id":663529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=663331#post663331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. I tend to avoid crossovers as well. Balance is just one issue. I also think that the themes of each game are damaged when you try to combine them.<br /> <br /> While each game line has all sorts of complex themes and reasons for players to interact, when you force them together often combat rises more to the forefront as it is a common activity which runs through every game line. That's is why combat balance becomes a bit more important in a crossover game than in most games individually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T00:32:08-07:00","id":664033,"title":"","content":"Since some time ago, my PnP Chronicles seem to be almost complete crossover.<br /> <br /> It all began, when I wanted to play a mere mortal, and tried to look up the ruleset for them. Since the mortal-rules were spread over several books (including every core-book), I started writing them together, innocently beliving, this would take a few hours at most.<br /> Since I was already going through each core book, I started adding the rules for Guhls, Kinfolk, Hedge-Magicians and those near mortals as well.<br /> Let me just say it spiraled out of control since there, and I`ve been writing on this &quot;book&quot; for the better part of 6 years now.<br /> <br /> I asked some of my friends, if they would meet with me for ocasional one-shots, trying out the rule-tweaks I`ve written together and testing how everything worked together.<br /> It led to some of the most awsome Hunter-Chronicles we`d ever played together and some of them still go on to this day.<br /> <br /> Once the rules for each &quot;Sub-Species&quot; (Guhles, Kinfolk etc.) including their potential magical abilities were finished, it was litterally a few hours of extra work to expand it into the full blown respective splatts.<br /> Now we play even fully awakend Groups with this crossover rule-book, and so far everything works out quite well.<br /> <br /> A month ago we started a Chronicle with an Imbuned Huntress, a Kami (think a Gaian-Fomori), a Changeling and an awakend Mage in brazil, with Pentex and a couple of Black Spiral Dancers as one of the main antagonists (they try to remove the village of the changeling and the kami to make way for an highway into the amazonas, and the huntress and the mage do have an old score to settle with the alpha Spiral, who is leading them).<br /> I know it sounds like a mess, but it works surprisingly well. Combat is hardly the focus of the chronicle till now, and the different splats are working off each other quite well.<br /> <br /> Going over every House-Rule or outright Rule-Change of this Crossover-Houserule-Book would take ages, but I am more than willing, on sending them per E-Mail, if there is interest for it.<br /> One word of caution though, its all written in german, so take that into acount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T13:29:13-07:00","id":667385,"title":"","content":"For the purposes of cross-overs, I tend to favor certain cross-overs more than others (a Mage can fit into any game--Vampires, not so much). However, for the purposes of hacking together a system, I lean very heavily on the Mage Storyteller's Handbook (Rev.), because it goes through great pains to establish a robust cross-over system in one of the appendices. And while it's far from perfect, it's an incredibly helpful and useful starting point. I would also like to add that I go to this book even when I'm not dealing with mages at all--this is because, absent two systems that plainly interact with one another seamlessly (e.g., the interaction between Auspex 1 <i>Heightened Senses</i>, and the Rank 1 Ragabash gift <i>Blur of the Milky Eye</i> comes to mind as an example of two disparate systems that perfectly work against one another in a well-defined tug-of-war), I use the crossover rules in the aforesaid Mage book as a sort of Rosetta stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T13:41:59-07:00","id":667396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=667385#post667385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the purposes of cross-overs, I tend to favor certain cross-overs more than others (a Mage can fit into any game--Vampires, not so much). However, for the purposes of hacking together a system, I lean very heavily on the Mage Storyteller's Handbook (Rev.), because it goes through great pains to establish a robust cross-over system in one of the appendices. And while it's far from perfect, it's an incredibly helpful and useful starting point. I would also like to add that I go to this book even when I'm not dealing with mages at all--this is because, absent two systems that plainly interact with one another seamlessly (e.g., the interaction between Auspex 1 <i>Heightened Senses</i>, and the Rank 1 Ragabash gift <i>Blur of the Milky Eye</i> comes to mind as an example of two disparate systems that perfectly work against one another in a well-defined tug-of-war), I use the crossover rules in the aforesaid Mage book as a sort of Rosetta stone.</div> </div> </div> </div>... you mean the same rules that posit that Rank 1 Gifts are equivalent to Level 1 Disciplines and level 1 Spheres? Seriously?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T16:32:56-08:00","id":771842,"title":"","content":"Well, <b>Asmodai</b>, I think that as a starting point he's right. They're crappy rules, but the only ones available from an official POV.<br /> <br /> The you get this starting point and go beyond, to something that really can almost work.<br /> <br /> My main concern in Crossovers, though, are the basic traits on the sheet that aren't consistent from a gameline to the next. Glamour/Banality is a tough one, but at least can be figured out without affecting the other things in any given character sheet. Faith Potential have some clear rules about how it works, but they are poor rules. A Demon in a Mage game will need to find creative ways to waist the helluva lot of Faith she will get from the Mages if they do the Pact... and they are simply worth enough thralls for the Ravaging being almost a non-issue.<br /> <br /> Virtues are worst, since when they show up they DO override some basic rules, the ones governing Willpower above all. And Demon using Virtues in a way while Vampire does another didn't helped it. My personal solution until now was to make any mortal follow Hunters Hunted rules as default, and have the splats using their own rules, but it IS suboptimal. I need a way to get Vampires and Demons on the same level as everyone else or give Virtues to everyone... and then I'll have to figure out what to do with Willpower inconsistencies.<br /> <br /> Abilities are the worst issue by far. They are more basic, and so they are more pervasive, but for the hell of it, they got more inconsistencies than any other trait. Some are completely redundant or simply too narrow, whyle others are very important except for not being on every line. Not to talk about the ones that are only ever rolled because there are powers based on them.<br /> <br /> I'm trying hard now to work around it. For now I have done with some friends a new list of 30 habilities. It is a start, but far from what I want for crossovers:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>TALENTS</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>SKILLS</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>KNOWLEDGE</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Alertness</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Animal Ken</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Computer</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Athletics</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Drive</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Investigation</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Brawl</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Etiquette</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Medicine</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dodge</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Firearms</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Occult</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Empathy</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Melee</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Politics</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Intimidation</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Perform</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Science</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Streetwise</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Crafts</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Law</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Subterfuge</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Stealth</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Academics</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Awareness</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Survivor</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Culture</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Sleight-of-Hand</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Larceny</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Cosmology</td> </tr> </table></div> Ever ask something that don't go in one of those, and it is remade to go in one of those anyway, or taken as Secondary Ability if not too relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T03:53:31-08:00","id":772206,"title":"","content":"Sidenote:<br /> I dont have massive experience with nWoD (frankly, removing the metaplot just makes it bland, and all the Covens, but especially Circle of the Crone make me want to punch somebody), but from what I have heard, its much more friendly to crossovers, with a more streamlined and common ability/damage/etc mechanic and pool.<br /> <br /> Is this true? If so, headaches may be saved by translating into nWoD mechanics and using those to Xover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T07:45:02-08:00","id":772297,"title":"","content":"Well, I play in a Mage/Werewolf crossover with a single Guipsy. The later one she tends to be the most problematic, ruleswise, because... face it: the rules in THAT splatbook are just... carps: Fish that eat what the others leave after eating the good stuff and/or dying.<br /> <br /> As far as Mage/Werewolf interaction goes: we chose the simnple way: all the mages have to buy Kinfolk, and we 2 are somewhat safe...well, at least me, the Verbena might turn out to be used as breeding stock at some point, but that is simply roleplay (and with her life stat, she might control that issiue to some degree). But ruleswise... We handle combat after the W20 rules, unless vehicles are involved (M20) or the mages start messing with mind/time magic to mess with turn order... as in... we speed up the Ahroun with time 3 for 2 extra rounds (which means she ages triple those moments), then the garou decides to spend 1 Rage in each of those rounds that exist in the moments between the rounds for the rest of the world, resulting in 6(+) actions for our raging beast of war while the enemies are more or less frozen in time... Alternatively: freeze the minds of the enemies to stillstand, resulting in the Garou... you see: The crossover of Mages and Werewolfs can be pretty deadly for enemies, unless they have some sort of magic defense - but our GM is wicked when it comes to enemies: we tend to be better off with not killing them because he has a pretty nasty Karmic whip... Which is a thing to keep in mind when coming to crossovers: some powers stack in very quite deadly/wicked/funny ways, which is only limited by player ingenuity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T07:53:03-08:00","id":772303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=772206#post772206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidenote:<br /> I dont have massive experience with nWoD (frankly, removing the metaplot just makes it bland, and all the Covens, but especially Circle of the Crone make me want to punch somebody), but from what I have heard, its much more friendly to crossovers, with a more streamlined and common ability/damage/etc mechanic and pool.<br /> <br /> Is this true? If so, headaches may be saved by translating into nWoD mechanics and using those to Xover.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's because everything is set up in exactly the same way, having a central power stat and fuel stat very similar to Generation and Blood Pool. Classic doesn't do this, as the games are going for different themes and experiences, so you'll have to be very careful about lining up unique stats and various powers. Especially Gifts, which are on a roller-coaster of effectiveness in a variety of ways and often don't maintain uniform level assignment across Garou and Fera; accordingly, Gift level shouldn't be used for anything (I keep repeating it because people seem keen to do it anyway)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T05:11:12-08:00","id":772975,"title":"","content":"I did a bunch of things, borrowing from NWoD copiously, both mechanically and setting wise. The primary thing was to use the mechanics in Kindred Of The East, since it is by far the most crossover friendly of the CWoD which is most crossover unfriendly. I also used the houserules on The Howling Void blog, by poster I Hate All Life(Hi Steven, your the man)<br /> <br /> Everyone has a Hun, Po, Yin and Yang stat or equivalent. This means splats without these stats must get them assigned.<br /> <br /> All of the above stats are either made equivalent with an existing stat, if no stat is suitable they must be assigned such a stat. Shifters have given me the most trouble here as well as changelings<br /> <br /> Every splat must have a power stat, or have one assigned, Generation = Dharma = Rankx2 =Faith etc. Shifters give me trouble again as well as changelings.<br /> <br /> Every splat must be given the ability to spontaneously cast minor effects of their disciplines/lores etc at an increased cost. Pick two attributes, subtract the rating of the effect, and pay power pts equal to the effect. Shifters are again an issue here, till my player suggested that totems, those spirits who teach specific gifts, could be assigned portfolios and ratings therein to get such spont abilities, i agreed to it, and he's doing all the homework so yay.<br /> <br /> Every power must be resistible if cast on another splat. Characters can either use an existing power to defend, or make a Power Block. by rolling their power stat equivalent in extremis.<br /> <br /> Mages get two successes for every one a non mage gets in an effect roll or defense, but this evens out since Non mages can have larger dice pools to counter.<br /> <br /> Extra Damage Successes from an attack roll is capped at stat or 10, which ever is lower.<br /> <br /> Theres a bunch of other stuff too but that the biggest part i think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:45:56-08:00","id":773103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=772975#post772975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a bunch of things, borrowing from NWoD copiously, both mechanically and setting wise. The primary thing was to use the mechanics in Kindred Of The East, since it is by far the most crossover friendly of the CWoD which is most crossover unfriendly. I also used the houserules on The Howling Void blog, by poster I Hate All Life(Hi Steven, your the man)<br /> <br /> Everyone has a Hun, Po, Yin and Yang stat or equivalent. This means splats without these stats must get them assigned.<br /> <br /> All of the above stats are either made equivalent with an existing stat, if no stat is suitable they must be assigned such a stat. Shifters have given me the most trouble here as well as changelings<br /> <br /> Every splat must have a power stat, or have one assigned, Generation = Dharma = Rankx2 =Faith etc. Shifters give me trouble again as well as changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of self-imposed, there. No one ever had to use Rank as an equivalent to a power stat, since it's equivalent to the Status Backgrounds from various other games that describe your place in a hierarchy; more akin to Title from Changeling, for example. The closest you get to power stats, most Changers will have two examples of, Rage and Gnosis.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:58:52-08:00","id":773173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=773103#post773103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kind of self-imposed, there. No one ever had to use Rank as an equivalent to a power stat, since it's equivalent to the Status Backgrounds from various other games that describe your place in a hierarchy; more akin to Title from Changeling, for example. The closest you get to power stats, most Changers will have two examples of, Rage and Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah its true and i tried that, but to my mind Rage and Gnosis dont regulate access to Gifts, the way generation or dharma limits discipline levels. So i went with that.<br /> <br /> Tbh, you were right Saur Ops, to make a crossover game work, WtA gets shafted, both in terms of setting mechanics and themes/fluff. My shifter player and i managed to find a good compromise but its obvious to us that he's disadvantaged, not in terms of power but by making shifter concerns fit the setting as crossover. Next time NWoD i swear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T14:48:30-08:00","id":773441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=773173#post773173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah its true and i tried that, but to my mind Rage and Gnosis dont regulate access to Gifts, the way generation or dharma limits discipline levels. So i went with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, those don't limit Disciplines and other Traits, it's just that having a super-high one makes you blatantly superhuman. Which Garou and Fera already are in other forms. Meanwhile, Fu Xi's Honor/Rage of the Nest Mother and similar effects can key off of permanent Renown ratings to obscene effect, even at low Rank. There are also other, weirder setups to that with other Traits or circumstances. Really, the other games are just too rigid about it, and it's a design choice that's been quite justifiably criticized, since it makes one Trait worth far more than the others in chargen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tbh, you were right Saur Ops, to make a crossover game work, WtA gets shafted, both in terms of setting mechanics and themes/fluff. My shifter player and i managed to find a good compromise but its obvious to us that he's disadvantaged, not in terms of power but by making shifter concerns fit the setting as crossover. Next time NWoD i swear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see the nWoD as a solution for the issue since it just puts a power stat in where it didn't need to be, but it is your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T07:12:09-08:00","id":773925,"title":"","content":"It depends whether you care about game balance or making the rules mesh. The former is harder, so I try not to worry about it too much. <br /> <br /> If it means that mages are suddenly less powerful and werewolves are suddenly more evenly matched, that isn't a flaw in my eyes.<br /> <br /> The important thing to remember is that PCs should be able to stand up to each other while still shining in their own right. For NPCs it doesn't matter, so you can just do away with their innate countermagick and cinematic soak if it isn't important for a particular encounter.<br /> <br /> Flexibility is key. If your mage is too squishy, give him armour or cool gadgets. If your mortal hunter is underpowered, let him develop True Faith or take a Merit that brings him up to scratch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 11-25-2015, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T22:43:28-08:00","id":777012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=772206#post772206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidenote:<br /> I dont have massive experience with nWoD (frankly, removing the metaplot just makes it bland, and all the Covens, but especially Circle of the Crone make me want to punch somebody), but from what I have heard, its much more friendly to crossovers, with a more streamlined and common ability/damage/etc mechanic and pool.<br /> <br /> Is this true? If so, headaches may be saved by translating into nWoD mechanics and using those to Xover.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, and a fair number of people do precisely that. But again, it is suboptimal. The rules in nWoD are meant for nWoD, and they don't represent perfectly the cWoD setting. Also, some people just don't like them (though many for simple prejudice). Anyway, there are no reason to not try to improve the rules of the cWoD.<br /> <br /> I already ceased to try for balance in cWoD, at least until 4th ed comes. But the real problem for me is really those inconsistent rules, when you don't know how to roll something because each line say to do different stuff, or when one splat get the short end not because of its inherent characteristics, but because the other's power calls for a roll of an Ability it doesn't have in the sheet to begin with, or because each line uses distinct traits for the same result. Again, a great problem with Virtues.<br /> <br /> But I don't think that the best solution will be a drastic change in most supernaturals. Mostly because I play with cWoD rules for the uniqueness of each splat, and to change them too much it would be easier to go for nWoD (what I actually do sometimes). Its far easier to use the Conversion Guides or just play nWoD than to hack cWoD until it becomes nWoD-like anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T12:47:46-08:00","id":777306,"title":"","content":"As I see it making such a system balanced would be near impossible and would only serve to undermine each system. As far as themes go I thing otherworldly horror like the quasi-cthulhuian mythos like in DTF would provide a good middle ground for themes as is allows for moments of personal horror like vampire(ancient gods eating your sanity), the moment of dramatic action like werewolf(fighting beings from beyond), the trans-humanism of mage(studying inhuman knowledge), and the depressive atmosphere of wraith(the slow destructive erosion of the world before your very eye's).<br /> <br /> The larger problem I can see are the interactions with spirits, as each game has their own interpretation for how they work. In past cross-playthroughs we ruled that spirits have different powers based around where they come from, a high umbral spirit will have powers like that of a mage as the high umbra is a realm of concepts and ideas, the middle umbral spirits have charms and gifts as the middle umbra is made of reflections of our world, the low umbra spirits have powers like wraiths or the thaumaturgy of vampires as they reflect memories of things that have passed, and the deep umbral spirits are much like fallen having sat at the edge of creation being corrupted by the abyss.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I don't mess with the systems as they are. A werewolf may be stronger than a vampire in straight combat, but that's because vampires aren't Supposed to be in straight combat all the time, they shine most when they manipulate from the shadows. A 1st rank werewolf straight from character creation may be able to take on a master vampire in open combat, but a newly embraced vampire can manipulate a city with blood alone and a matter of weeks what it would take a 5th rank garou with the most socially oriented gifts Years to accomplish.<br /> <br /> Each system has it's own merits, and using those merit's properly with a group of good roleplayers can make for Delicious conflict and amazing stories. If some players fall behind because they can't use those talents it's on them, not the system. Sure it's not balanced, but nether is real life and WOD works best when it reflects real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:10:11-08:00","id":778623,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, like several others, I borrowed the &quot;key mystical attribute acts as resistance bonus to supernatural powers&quot; and simply house-ruled Blood Potency into VtM (I have some complicated house rules for revamping VtM's Kindred).<br /> <br /> As far as lore, I simply pick which line is &quot;dominant&quot;, and that canon rules over the others. Chiefly, I run either Vampire or Mage. Garou, Wraiths, and Changelings exist, but if there's a dispute between Mage Umbra and Werewolf Umbra, Mage Umbra wins and the Garou Umbra gets either a retcon or a handwave of why things are different.<br /> <br /> If Vampire is dominant, then the Technocracy is a small but powerful conspiracy that operates behind the bureaucracy of the modern world, while vampire elders hold the immediate power. If Mage is dominant, then the Technocracy is the Secret Government manipulating events, while the vampires are the small but powerful conspiracy that manipulates power indirecty to avoid drawing NWO's attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 12-02-2015, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T17:42:31-08:00","id":778717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=778623#post778623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically, like several others, I borrowed the &quot;key mystical attribute acts as resistance bonus to supernatural powers&quot; and simply house-ruled Blood Potency into VtM (I have some complicated house rules for revamping VtM's Kindred).<br /> <br /> As far as lore, I simply pick which line is &quot;dominant&quot;, and that canon rules over the others. Chiefly, I run either Vampire or Mage. Garou, Wraiths, and Changelings exist, but if there's a dispute between Mage Umbra and Werewolf Umbra, Mage Umbra wins and the Garou Umbra gets either a retcon or a handwave of why things are different.<br /> <br /> If Vampire is dominant, then the Technocracy is a small but powerful conspiracy that operates behind the bureaucracy of the modern world, while vampire elders hold the immediate power. If Mage is dominant, then the Technocracy is the Secret Government manipulating events, while the vampires are the small but powerful conspiracy that manipulates power indirecty to avoid drawing NWO's attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not weave the conspiracies together, if both exist why wouldn't the syndicate have shares in pentex? less werewolves is something they can definitely get behind. Would it really be a surprise if the technocracy was also backing the camarilla? Them enforcing the masquerade on themselves is far better for the consensus than mages and vampires battling in the streets. Why wouldn't void engineers work with weaver drones? them reinforcing the gauntlet not only keeps out the reality deviants, but also makes it easier for them to use dimensional science.<br /> <br /> In a cross-over I find it easier to group together teams with similar goals, they may not go out of their way to help each other(a technocrat won't go out of his way to stop you killing a powerful vamp, it just means one less loose end and more access to its business shares. However if you start making things obvious and threaten the consensus, the technocrat will not only be on the vampires side for the fight(much easier than fighting both you and the vamp) he'll help frame you afterward on the local news(maintaining the consensus and the vamp gets to use the incident to up his social standing as an underdog hero.) It keeps players on their toes as they can be attacked from all sides at any time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T18:51:12-08:00","id":778742,"title":"","content":"I do that, but in my own revamped &quot;World of Insufficient Illumination&quot; version of the setting. Basically, I tend to run my games with less Lovecraft or Kafka and more Butcher. <br /> <br /> In that setting, that Technocracy is what's infiltrated the intelligence apparatus and commercial sectors. The Camarilla is deeply entrenched in the civilian government. Both can manipulate the military when necessary but have to keep direct hands off thanks to a Task Force Valkyrie style group that's been around since World War II that tends to... purge direct infiltrators pretty quickly. Pentex is just a Nephandi corrupted branch of the Syndicate. <br /> <br /> Vampires and Werewolves are not at war, but neither do they like each other very much. The Garou divide their time between keeping the spirit world and physical world from corrupting each other until they're ready to re-merge, and stopping their brethren who've lost themselves to the Rage and want to wipe out the modern world.<br /> <br /> The Tradition Council remains largely the same, though more unified. <br /> <br /> The Abyss has not been breached, instead angelic beings have been cast out of Heaven and are forced to merge with creatures they once thought beneath them. Some are adapting, some are in denial, and others have gone mad, thinking the only way they'll find release is if the world ends, so they're trying to find ways to make it happen sooner rather than later. <br /> <br /> Wraith is largely unchanged. Changeling... I feel neither published version works well with my setting, and haven't had the time to come up with something new, so they're strictly NPCs. I tend to run them as powerful spirits that are more humanlike in some aspects but with vastly alien mindsets and persepctives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 12-02-2015, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T16:56:56-08:00","id":779362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=778742#post778742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do that, but in my own revamped &quot;World of Insufficient Illumination&quot; version of the setting. Basically, I tend to run my games with less Lovecraft or Kafka and more Butcher.<br /> <br /> In that setting, that Technocracy is what's infiltrated the intelligence apparatus and commercial sectors. The Camarilla is deeply entrenched in the civilian government. Both can manipulate the military when necessary but have to keep direct hands off thanks to a Task Force Valkyrie style group that's been around since World War II that tends to... purge direct infiltrators pretty quickly. Pentex is just a Nephandi corrupted branch of the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> Vampires and Werewolves are not at war, but neither do they like each other very much. The Garou divide their time between keeping the spirit world and physical world from corrupting each other until they're ready to re-merge, and stopping their brethren who've lost themselves to the Rage and want to wipe out the modern world.<br /> <br /> The Tradition Council remains largely the same, though more unified.<br /> <br /> The Abyss has not been breached, instead angelic beings have been cast out of Heaven and are forced to merge with creatures they once thought beneath them. Some are adapting, some are in denial, and others have gone mad, thinking the only way they'll find release is if the world ends, so they're trying to find ways to make it happen sooner rather than later.<br /> <br /> Wraith is largely unchanged. Changeling... I feel neither published version works well with my setting, and haven't had the time to come up with something new, so they're strictly NPCs. I tend to run them as powerful spirits that are more humanlike in some aspects but with vastly alien mindsets and persepctives.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meh, lovecraft for life. :P<br /> <br /> I personally try to go with settings where I change as little as possible as to preserve the individuals themes of each book. multi-leveled conspiracies and ancient horrors seem to blend those themes best(though it does mean some stories end up in settings that wouldn't be out of place as a level in Bloodborne.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T18:49:09-08:00","id":779437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=779362#post779362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Meh, lovecraft for life. :P<br /> <br /> I personally try to go with settings where I change as little as possible as to preserve the individuals themes of each book. multi-leveled conspiracies and ancient horrors seem to blend those themes best(though it does mean some stories end up in settings that wouldn't be out of place as a level in Bloodborne.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been playing since '94. I'm bored with the RAW as far as settings go. WoD got more and more oppressive and restrictive with each edition in what Storytellers were &quot;allowed&quot; to do if they wanted to follow the metaplot. There are two types of NPCs, with few exceptions. They're talked up as epic badasses, but with a stat block that's comparatively weak (which works because the advancement system is designed around chronicles that last years in order to see any real advancement). Look no further than the maturation rules in any Vampire edition to see how laughably weak &quot;elders&quot; are. My favorite example, though, are ghouls. A couple splats talk about about how some vampire ghouled his men (exact number unknown, but implied to be a decent sized strike force at bare minimum) before a battle and turned them into an unstoppable force. Yeah, 1 dot of Potence really turns your men into an unholy wrecking crew. And unless this guy was 4th gen and emptied his entire Blood Pool into them, they didn't even have enough in their system to HEAL much less fuel that single dot for any length of time.<br /> <br /> The other type are SO POWERFUL THEY SIMPLY WIN!!!! See Antediluvians, Oracles, True Fae, and assorted others. At first that didn't bother me, because as they say &quot;if you stat it, they will kill it.&quot; So, if they're so godlike, why isn't the REAL war between them, fighting for ultimate control with starting level PCs as pawns? &quot;Because, they don't get involved!&quot; Why would beings with such power not use it, especially vampires and mages? &quot;Because the rules won't let them!&quot; ... Whatever.<br /> <br /> But towards the end of CWoD, I had a realization. The regime that had taken over WW were AFRAID of players. They didn't stat the Epic NPCs, because that would risk players DEFEATING them. Not just slaying them BUT BEATING THEM, which meant they'd have effectively changed the setting in a definitive manner. Can't have that! But then look at the NPCs, so powerful in fluff but pathetic in stat form. Each Edition talked more and more of how this supernatural faction or another couldn't affect REAL change and how all they did was ride human trends and manipulate the masses into passivity. Even the Technocracy got hit with this. They had all the makings of an interesting Alternative History if not in the past, then at least diverging into one, and they refused to use it, bending believabilty as they reached for bigger and bigger excuses for why mages, vampires, and werewolves existed, but had absolutely ZERO impact on the world at large, even from the shadows.<br /> <br /> The final piece was the advancement system. I'd always accepted that WoD games were meant to be long-term things, and the system was designed around. But then I noticed how few people ran games that lasted longer than a year (at least in my neck of the woods). None of their characters ever saw a fifth dot in ANYTHING, unless they devoted every drop of XP they got to raising it, and they did that by barely advancing in anything else. The system STRANGLED choice, meaning you min-maxed your character for your desired role at chargen, and then never spent XP except to advance in that role. Any attempt at adding variety or purely &quot;RP&quot; choices was thrown aside, because unless you lucked out and got into a Mega-Campaign, you were never going be much more than what you were at the start.<br /> <br /> At the time, I broached this in the old WW forums, and got lambasted for not &quot;Getting it,&quot; and &quot;not understanding that being powerful and affecting change goes against the themes of WoD.&quot; That's pretty much when I burned WoD's canon and reforged my own. My ultimate vindication was seeing Vampire the Requeim 2nd Edition go for an XP system very similar to the one I came up nearly a decade before. Onyx Path seems to be taking a more moderate stance with the Edition Agnostic 20th line, and I'm VERY curious to see what they do with VtM 4th Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 12-03-2015, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T09:41:29-08:00","id":779887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=779437#post779437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been playing since '94. I'm bored with the RAW as far as settings go...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well one thing to prove this is is when you take two NPC's of the first type who are important to the plot of different stories and compare their backgrounds, take one elder vampire who's been around since the dark ages gathering allies and influence since before the printing press and then take a vampire who was only embraced five years prior, but is important in a local town. Now notice the fact they have nearly the same number of dots in backgrounds.<br /> <br /> My friends and I have found so many cases of this throughout WOD settings that it's somewhat of a joke. It was also the last straw for me that made me scrap the XP system all together and focused on roleplaying alone. I run it as any time you want to advance a dot in something you must find a teacher with that level and have them teach it to you, this means you have to find them, convince them to teach you, and study with for a few hours(this is represented by an intelligence plus empathy roll difficulty 9-10, you may only make once a day and in the prssence of your teacher) each success(botches remove stored successes) is counted as 1 Exp that you may only use to buy what your being taught.<br /> <br /> I gave all &quot;They win&quot; NPC's stats hat made sense. Caine is the same power as an ante(10 dots in all 8 &quot;Basic&quot; disciplines, blood magic, and their unique clan discipline) just older(10 dots in all unique clan disciplines) and with gods curse/blessing(any time caine takes damage, his attacker also suffers (their damage x7) levels of (attackers damage type)damage. You know, the 7 fold thing from the bible.).<br /> <br /> Lucifer and the earthbound archdukes are just powerful fallen(10 faith + 5 dots in all lore for lucifer, 10 faith + 5 dots in most lores for the archdukes(depend on archduke, also in my games I run demon lores as more akin to mages spheres or the true faith merit then how their written as they otherwise don't fit the powers their said to have in the meta) I also changed the Eminence so that it affected stats and apocalyptic form of the fallen(as having the book say in meta that the reason a demon is unable to escape the abyss is that it's vast power and enormous apocalyptic form, yet then give no real stat difference between them is, as my friend coined the term, bull-fluff.) So now instead of all fallen having 16 apocalyptic trait points for 8 apocalyptic traits, they now get (eminence^eminence) trait points for (eminence x2) traits, earthbound are also able to raise their urges up to(5 or their eminence, whichever is higher).<br /> 1-5 same as in book<br /> 6 abyssal baron<br /> 7 abyssal duke<br /> 8 the archdukes<br /> 9 lucifer.<br /> 10 god(Note: eminence has no stat advantages to this NPC, not that it matters)<br /> <br /> Oracles I always used the sphere 6 as described in the back of horizon 2nd edition(note: I deny arch-mages ever existed), but with lower difficulties(I ignore the books listed difficulties and instead determine difficulties based on the situation. Nothing is impossible, some things are just difficulty 25).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 12-04-2015, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T13:25:38-08:00","id":780093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=777306#post777306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see it making such a system balanced would be near impossible and would only serve to undermine each system. As far as themes go I thing otherworldly horror like the quasi-cthulhuian mythos like in DTF would provide a good middle ground for themes as is allows for moments of personal horror like vampire(ancient gods eating your sanity), the moment of dramatic action like werewolf(fighting beings from beyond), the trans-humanism of mage(studying inhuman knowledge), and the depressive atmosphere of wraith(the slow destructive erosion of the world before your very eye's).<br /> <br /> The larger problem I can see are the interactions with spirits, as each game has their own interpretation for how they work. In past cross-playthroughs we ruled that spirits have different powers based around where they come from, a high umbral spirit will have powers like that of a mage as the high umbra is a realm of concepts and ideas, the middle umbral spirits have charms and gifts as the middle umbra is made of reflections of our world, the low umbra spirits have powers like wraiths or the thaumaturgy of vampires as they reflect memories of things that have passed, and the deep umbral spirits are much like fallen having sat at the edge of creation being corrupted by the abyss.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I don't mess with the systems as they are. A werewolf may be stronger than a vampire in straight combat, but that's because vampires aren't Supposed to be in straight combat all the time, they shine most when they manipulate from the shadows. A 1st rank werewolf straight from character creation may be able to take on a master vampire in open combat, but a newly embraced vampire can manipulate a city with blood alone and a matter of weeks what it would take a 5th rank garou with the most socially oriented gifts Years to accomplish.<br /> <br /> Each system has it's own merits, and using those merit's properly with a group of good roleplayers can make for Delicious conflict and amazing stories. If some players fall behind because they can't use those talents it's on them, not the system. Sure it's not balanced, but nether is real life and WOD works best when it reflects real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll set aside my disagreement on the matter of balance (it is too complex, and not for this thread), and that cWoD reflects real life as much as D&amp;D. The problem isn't balance, but inconsistencies in mechanics that make the rules' interactions too hard to judge in a crossover game.<br /> <br /> By the way, I also modified the XP system to something more like nWoD 2nd Ed. But simply throwing greater amounts of XP also does the trick to some degree. I didn't found my perfect system for any of this, though. Your ideas for some changes are very interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T18:39:22-08:00","id":780294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=779887#post779887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well one thing to prove this is is when you take two NPC's of the first type who are important to the plot of different stories and compare their backgrounds, take one elder vampire who's been around since the dark ages gathering allies and influence since before the printing press and then take a vampire who was only embraced five years prior, but is important in a local town. Now notice the fact they have nearly the same number of dots in backgrounds.<br /> <br /> My friends and I have found so many cases of this throughout WOD settings that it's somewhat of a joke. It was also the last straw for me that made me scrap the XP system all together and focused on roleplaying alone. I run it as any time you want to advance a dot in something you must find a teacher with that level and have them teach it to you, this means you have to find them, convince them to teach you, and study with for a few hours(this is represented by an intelligence plus empathy roll difficulty 9-10, you may only make once a day and in the prssence of your teacher) each success(botches remove stored successes) is counted as 1 Exp that you may only use to buy what your being taught.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ONLY Written NPCs that were actually as powerful as their age would imply were Marcus Vitel of DC By Night (and look what they did to him; see my rant below) and Khemintiri from the Kindred Most Wanted. They were actually statted out to be properly terrifying. My jaw dropped when I saw her reappear in &quot;Dread List.&quot; Gave me hope that OP might walk a different path. <br /> <br /> 2nd Edition tried to loosen the reigns a little and gave us books like &quot;Elysium&quot;, &quot;The Book of Worlds&quot;, &quot;Ascension's Right Hand&quot;,and other more controversial ones, that actually showed that there WERE power players that operated at a whole nother level in WoD and even gave Storytellers the option to run campaigns beyond just &quot;be a lowly peon forever struggling to make their way in a doomed world that crushes everyone under a non-caring heel.&quot; <br /> <br /> Then Revised came along, took very single one of those books and IMMEDIATELY disavowed them. The &quot;lucky&quot; ones had big event transpire to render them null and void. The less fortunate were just out and out retconned as invalid by new canon with no explanation given. I've never been an Edition Grognard before or since, but after awhile, i refused to acknowlege Revised sourcebooks as far as setting and metaplot went. I ran Second Edition games on Revised rules for years. I bought 20th because I liked the idea of an edition-agnostic Definitive Collection. If Achilli and his crew had announced 4th Edition, I wouldn't have even looked at it. Now that OP has taken over, I'm willing to give a new edition a fair shake. If I hate it, I can keep doing what I've been doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T18:46:21-08:00","id":780297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=780093#post780093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll set aside my disagreement on the matter of balance (it is too complex, and not for this thread), and that cWoD reflects real life as much as D&amp;D. The problem isn't balance, but inconsistencies in mechanics that make the rules' interactions too hard to judge in a crossover game.<br /> <br /> By the way, I also modified the XP system to something more like nWoD 2nd Ed. But simply throwing greater amounts of XP also does the trick to some degree. I didn't found my perfect system for any of this, though. Your ideas for some changes are very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such thing as &quot;balanced&quot; system, and more writers try to MAKE them balanced by shoving rule after rule down our throats, the less I like the game. It's the province of the STORYTELLER to keep things &quot;balanced&quot; so that the players can enjoy themselves and the narrative stay focused. Take for example, abominations. They made them APPALLINGLY awful and near worthless as even NPCs all so players wouldn't want to play them.<br /> <br /> Me, I chucked the horribly written Abomination and replaced it with something actually TERRIFYING, that both sides would want dead just for their own peace of mind. And when a player tries to hand me a background to be one, I laugh, pat them on the head, tell them &quot;nice try, now go make a real character&quot; and move on. If someone can't control their players without having a chapter and paragraph verse to reference to back up their rulings, then they have no business being behind the screen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 12-04-2015, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T19:08:59-08:00","id":780311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=780297#post780297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If someone can't control their players without having a chapter and paragraph verse to reference to back up their rulings, then they have no business being behind the screen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen, BTW can you pm me your abomination rules please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T20:37:19-08:00","id":780356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=780311#post780311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Amen, BTW can you pm me your abomination rules please?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would've asked that they just get posted somewhere. I'm curious too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T21:23:53-08:00","id":780375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=780356#post780356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would've asked that they just get posted somewhere. I'm curious too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm rebuilding my house rules, as my old Word doc got lost somewhere along the line. I'm rebuilding it now. I have a partial reconstruction posted in another thread, but it doesn't have the Abomination stuff in it yet. If you like, I can start a new thread with my various &quot;setting tweaks&quot; and &quot;house rules&quot;. I've had a couple other queries on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T22:46:26-08:00","id":780407,"title":"","content":"I always enjoy seeing the house rules people put together. It's interesting to me to see how people have used the setting or system to make their own custom games or stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T00:06:58-08:00","id":780428,"title":"","content":"A house rule that I am fond of is that a basic Investment that a Demon can offer is to grant a natural proficiency for sorcery to anyone who would otherwise not be able to achieve it. The failed sorcery student, after selling his soul for that investment and Occult 5 can now become the new prodigy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T04:07:35-08:00","id":780488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=780297#post780297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no such thing as &quot;balanced&quot; system, and more writers try to MAKE them balanced by shoving rule after rule down our throats, the less I like the game. It's the province of the STORYTELLER to keep things &quot;balanced&quot; so that the players can enjoy themselves and the narrative stay focused. Take for example, abominations. They made them APPALLINGLY awful and near worthless as even NPCs all so players wouldn't want to play them.<br /> <br /> Me, I chucked the horribly written Abomination and replaced it with something actually TERRIFYING, that both sides would want dead just for their own peace of mind. And when a player tries to hand me a background to be one, I laugh, pat them on the head, tell them &quot;nice try, now go make a real character&quot; and move on. If someone can't control their players without having a chapter and paragraph verse to reference to back up their rulings, then they have no business being behind the screen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, lets tackle this just a little...<br /> <br /> Usually the problem is what people call &quot;balance&quot;. The idea of a perfect equilibrium between characters, where each one have mathematical equivalence, is one such concept. I won't lose my time with it (though I did believed in it in the past, and I do believe in it <u>under adequate context</u>), this is a failed concept when taken to a broad analysis. The idea that balance somehow equates to rules for combat is another recurrent one, and I'm very tired of people arguing against balance saying that the game isn't about combat. To me this is just pure <i>non sequitur</i>. To say that balance necessarily means more and/or more complex rules is simply to make a lot of assumptions ahead of time.<br /> <br /> Balance is, first and foremost, a value, a judgement, and as such a subjective thing, not an objective phenomenon. Not to say that it can't be objectively analyzed, but as every subjective perception, only in context. And in an RPG game, the context is such that no player should sense that she took the worst end of the bargain without wanting it. Those are &quot;balancing issues&quot;, and balance should be studied and applied in the sense of creating a better gaming experience for everyone.<br /> <br /> Lets take the Abomination as an example. As RAW, it is a <b>huge</b> balance issue. It doesn't have nothing to do with its strength, however. Actually, it isn't even near to as strong as some people (and the fluff) seems to indicate. It is just a weakened werewolf with addition of Disciplines as a possibility (they still cost XP). But it is unplayable, in the sense that anyone trying to use it will have a very cumbersome experience. Too hard to do anything with it.<br /> <br /> Now, you want to use it just for NPCs? That's good enough for me, and it does means that balance is almost a non-issue. It still can play a role depending on how you want to use the character, because it have to do with how it will interact mechanically with the PCs, so the dice can translate adequately the intended fiction. But it isn't balance in the sense most people think of it.<br /> <br /> You want to let a PC be an Abomination? You don't have to, doesn't matter how much some people can argue about that. The RAW <u>should</u> make them usable, but not balanced for PCs. But using them as PCs is an equally valid decision, one that changes context. But in this new context, balance becomes a lot more relevant. It isn't about straight equivalence, but perceived equilibrium. If a player is given the choice between an Abomination, a vampire and a werewolf, the player have the right to sense that whatever choice he makes is a good one. Of course, some players will like the challenge to play a weaker or otherwise more limited character, and that's fine. But it shouldn't be the default assumption. D&amp;D 3E is a game with far more mathematical consistency and equivalence than cWoD, and even then it is remarkably plagued by balance issues because of false equivalences that make some choices simply more efficient than others, punishing a player for not knowing the game.<br /> <br /> I don't have hope for cWoD in this regard before 4th Ed, but I do have some for the future. I do think that a better balance can be achieved without sacrificing the game. Most people who are against it seem full of prejudice about what balance means, and somehow think that the result will be D&amp;D or nWoD. Those games are used as examples for being more balanced, not for being the only possibilities. I'm certainly against the fear some people have to make any modification in the game, going to such heights as to praise some of its flaws as if they where actually merits, like the recurrent and tiresome argument that &quot;unfairness makes the game more real&quot;. This simply isn't true in absolutely any way.<br /> <br /> About the rules on Abominations, I would like to see them. I didn't used them too much in my games, and when I did I simply took out some of its limitations, but I'm not saying that this is necessarily the best way to deal with them. It worked just fine for what I needed (even once being a PC), but they are far from the nightmarish horror they are purported to be. Again, the topic on hand as far as I remember is crossover rules, not balance itself, and Abominations are an interesting side-topic by being the defining result of crossover between two game lines. I would also like to see other stuff about &quot;hybrids&quot; of sorts.<br /> <br /> Someone here uses the rules about ghouled mages losing Arete without even a chance to avoid the loss? What about Mages or Fera being Demonic Thralls? Some of those materials are good enough already, but even those can have alternate possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T19:40:29-08:00","id":785706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=780488#post780488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someone here uses the rules about ghouled mages losing Arete without even a chance to avoid the loss? What about Mages or Fera being Demonic Thralls? Some of those materials are good enough already, but even those can have alternate possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're really into &quot;Hybrids&quot; the best places to look are &quot;Human&quot; runs(Ironically enough). Sorcerers(Alchemists in particular) are pretty crap when paired alone with mage, but become absolute beasts in crossovers as humans are the only creatures that can have multi-templates.<br /> <br /> (Example: a beginning sorcerer isn't much to look at, but throughout a play-through they can become ghouled, learn lores as a thrall, and make a deal with a spirit to become possessed without losing any of the previous powers. I also house-rule the achemy and enchantment paths so that if a sorcerer uses a certain potion that increases dots frequently, they can buy dots with experience permanently(as in if an alchemist has alchemy 5 and strength 5, as well as frequently uses a potion that make him strength 6, I'll allow him to buy strength 6 permanently for the normal experience cost.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T06:26:38-08:00","id":786684,"title":"","content":"My curiosity about those isn't just to make powerful characters. It is mainly a curiosity about the rules for interactions.<br /> <br /> Once you declare that more than one splat is using its own rules, some interactions have to be thought of, because they can occur. That's true even if the core of the chronicle, and the PCs, isn't a crossover itself.<br /> <br /> Your chronicle have Vampires and other splats? You have to think about the effects of the blood on each of those splats. What if a PC werewolf enters into a Demonic Pact? And when the Mage is Enchanted by a Changeling? More than any cosmological definition, those are the questions I find more interesting to explore in any sort of crossover of rules, because those are the questions that strengthen some assumptions of each splat, but can also jeopardize some of those assumptions, and even make for possibilities none had thought before. It creates questions about the nature of the WoD more than it answers them. Or it simply answers them when the ST finds it the best course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T11:55:53-08:00","id":786832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games?p=786684#post786684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My curiosity about those isn't just to make powerful characters. It is mainly a curiosity about the rules for interactions.<br /> <br /> Once you declare that more than one splat is using its own rules, some interactions have to be thought of, because they can occur. That's true even if the core of the chronicle, and the PCs, isn't a crossover itself.<br /> <br /> Your chronicle have Vampires and other splats? You have to think about the effects of the blood on each of those splats. What if a PC werewolf enters into a Demonic Pact? And when the Mage is Enchanted by a Changeling? More than any cosmological definition, those are the questions I find more interesting to explore in any sort of crossover of rules, because those are the questions that strengthen some assumptions of each splat, but can also jeopardize some of those assumptions, and even make for possibilities none had thought before. It creates questions about the nature of the WoD more than it answers them. Or it simply answers them when the ST finds it the best course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's why I suggested sorcerer, because it allows you to base a story around these elements easily. The idea of &quot;Mixed Magic&quot; is something I personally love talking about in stories as it allows for a story that would otherwise be rather simple and generic to become a surprising thriller that would keep even veteran players on their toes.<br /> <br /> What happens when one combines the rituals and ritae of the blood with the gifts and rites of the BSD? What happens when a changeling interferes in a thaumaturge's ritual? What happens when you mix linear and dynamic magics? The possibilities are endless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T21:47:35-07:00","id":875263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661921-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossover-games#post661921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What house rules do you use to make multi-species games workable/balanced?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found its easier to pick one side to make 'prominent' then draw in the others. Such as often when i did vamp/garou crosses, i would either put vamp as dominant and draw in were stuff, OR put werewolf dominant and draw in vamp side.. The biggest Imo balancer is, you can't make it where one side though is too potent over the other, otherwise no one would wanna play them...<br /> <br /> As an example of one of the rules i have used in the past.. Vampires who try to use Presence on a Fera who is berserked, risks going enraged themselves if they botch their power check, where as using dominate on one so enraged, incurrs a +2 difficulty penalty to activate the power..<br /> <br /> Some of the bigger issues i have come across through out the years, is gifts vs disciplines vs power ranks for mages and such..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}